<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
     AresLauncher: letter section header (A / B / C) for the app-list pane.

     Ares-owned rather than a shared layout: BaseAllAppsAdapter serves the Taskbar's all-apps
     sheet and the secondary-display host as well as our pane, and editing shared all-apps
     layouts in place has already caused silent collateral damage twice (the Discover feed, and
     the Taskbar being forced single-column). This file is inflated only for
     VIEW_TYPE_ARES_SECTION_HEADER, which is only ever produced behind
     AresAllApps.isAresAppListPane(), so stock surfaces never reach it.

     Visual intent (design/implementation-scope.md §8, Niagara traits 3-4): the letter is a
     signpost, not content. Smaller and dimmer than the 17sp app labels it groups, on a shorter
     row, so the list still reads as sparse and text-forward rather than gaining chrome.

     textColor resolves against the wallpaper via workspaceTextColor for the same reason the row
     layout does: since the CONVERGENCE TARGET restyle the pane draws directly on the wallpaper
     with no sheet behind it, so the style default (textColorSecondary, which assumes an opaque
     light sheet) renders dark-on-dark. alpha de-emphasises it without a second colour attribute,
     which would have to be resolved against the wallpaper all over again.
-->
<TextView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/ares_section_header"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="@dimen/ares_section_header_height"
    android:alpha="0.6"
    android:ellipsize="end"
    android:gravity="start|bottom"
    android:maxLines="1"
    android:paddingStart="@dimen/ares_app_row_padding_horizontal"
    android:paddingTop="@dimen/ares_section_header_padding_top"
    android:paddingEnd="@dimen/ares_app_row_padding_horizontal"
    android:textAllCaps="true"
    android:textColor="?attr/workspaceTextColor"
    android:textSize="@dimen/ares_section_header_text_size"
    android:textStyle="bold" />
